## Architecture

<p align="center">
  <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Frontend-HTML%20%C2%B7%20CSS%20%C2%B7%20JavaScript-f8fafc?style=flat-square&color=4f46e5" />
  <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Backend-Node.js%20%C2%B7%20Express-f8fafc?style=flat-square&color=4338ca" />
  <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Database-Supabase%20PostgreSQL-f8fafc?style=flat-square&color=06b6d4" />
  <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Storage-Supabase%20Storage-f8fafc?style=flat-square&color=0891b2" />
  <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/AI-Ollama%20%28GCP%29-f8fafc?style=flat-square&color=10b981" />
  <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Hosting-Vercel-f8fafc?style=flat-square&color=6366f1" />
</p>

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| **Frontend** | HTML, CSS, JavaScript — role-based portals with a shared design system |
| **Backend** | Node.js, Express — REST API with JWT authentication |
| **Database** | Supabase (PostgreSQL) — profiles, jobs, applications, AI analyses |
| **Storage** | Supabase Storage — résumés and applicant documents |
| **AI** | Ollama — cloud-hosted inference with configurable models |
| **Deployment** | Vercel (application) · Google Cloud (AI inference) |

The API serves the frontend, orchestrates auth, persists hiring data, and coordinates document extraction and model inference. Employer-scoped queries ensure jobs and applicants remain tied to the account that owns them.

---

## Design Philosophy

> RecruitIQ is built around **clarity** and **accountability** in hiring.

Requirements are explicit. Scores cite application content. The interface separates public marketing, authenticated portals, and employer tooling without conflating roles. The platform is intended to feel professional, fast, and trustworthy — the kind of system a hiring team can rely on daily.

